
# Windows PC Boot Loop Troubleshooting

## 📌 Project Overview

This project documents my experience troubleshooting a Windows PC that experienced a boot loop and could not start normally.

I used Windows recovery tools, Safe Mode, and an older system backup to restore the computer to a working state.

## 🎯 Objectives

- Troubleshoot a Windows boot loop
- Access Windows Recovery Environment
- Boot Windows into Safe Mode
- Restore the system using an older backup
- Develop practical troubleshooting and system recovery skills

## 🛠️ Tools & Technologies

- Windows
- Windows Recovery Environment
- Safe Mode
- System Backup / Restore

## 🔧 Troubleshooting Process

### 1. Problem Identification

The PC experienced a boot loop that prevented it from starting normally.

The issue was associated with a suspected hardware-related problem.

### 2. Accessing Recovery Mode

I accessed Windows Recovery Mode to troubleshoot the startup issue.

### 3. Booting into Safe Mode

I started the computer in Safe Mode to access Windows with a minimal set of drivers and services.

### 4. System Restoration

I restored the computer using an older backup to return the system to a previously working state.

## ✅ Results

The troubleshooting process successfully resolved the boot loop, and the PC was restored to a working condition.

## 📚 Lessons Learned

- Gained experience accessing Windows Recovery Environment
- Practiced booting Windows into Safe Mode
- Learned how system restoration can help recover a computer
- Improved my understanding of Windows troubleshooting workflows

## 🚀 Future Improvements

- Learn additional Windows startup repair techniques
- Practice diagnosing hardware-related boot problems
- Explore Windows diagnostic and recovery tools in a controlled lab environment
